Third-party components
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

The Go modules in this repository (`dashboard/`, `pustaka/`) depend on the Go
standard library only and vendor no third-party Go code — neither has a
`go.sum`. See `README.md`.

  * The Elephant-Goldfish Model ......... Apache License 2.0
    https://github.com/google/elephant-goldfish-model
    The design-gate method in `docs/rules/gaos-design-review.md`, its
    five-lens reviewer structure and its document standards. Not a
    supported Google product.

  * The Emil Kowalski design skills ...... MIT License
    https://github.com/emilkowalski/skill
    `break-ui`, `review-animations` and `emil-design-eng`, vendored under
    .claude/skills/ at commit f1090bec277140d02ed202440185ad9d02ac1490.
    `emil-design-eng` is a GAOS-modified edition: the upstream file with its
    motion, framework and duplicate-craft sections cut, recorded in its
    SOURCE.md.

The documentation site vendors self-hosted web fonts and one JavaScript library,
each under its own licence, in `pustaka/docs/assets/`:

  * Atkinson Hyperlegible ....... SIL Open Font License 1.1
  * Bricolage Grotesque ......... SIL Open Font License 1.1
  * JetBrains Mono .............. SIL Open Font License 1.1
  * Apache ECharts .............. Apache License 2.0

ECharts embeds BSD 3-Clause code from d3 in four of its own source files, and
carries the TypeScript runtime helpers under their Microsoft permission grant.

The full licence text of each sits beside the files it covers — retaining them
is an obligation of redistribution, not a courtesy:

  * pustaka/docs/assets/fonts/LICENSE-atkinson-hyperlegible.txt
  * pustaka/docs/assets/fonts/LICENSE-bricolage-grotesque.txt
  * pustaka/docs/assets/fonts/LICENSE-jetbrains-mono.txt
  * pustaka/docs/assets/vendor/LICENSE-echarts.txt
  * pustaka/docs/assets/vendor/NOTICE-echarts.txt   (Apache 2.0 section 4(d))
  * pustaka/docs/assets/vendor/LICENSE-d3.txt

Each was fetched from its upstream project rather than reconstructed; the two
`README.md` files in those directories record the version, the source and the
digest, so what is vendored can be shown to be what was published. The Microsoft
grant is complete inside `echarts.min.js` itself, which is why the bundle is
vendored verbatim and never re-minified. `deploy/check-stacks.sh` asserts that
nothing here ships without its licence.

Nothing in this repository transmits data to a third party at build or render
time. Where GAOS sends data anywhere at run time — to a model provider, on the
operator's own account — is documented in `pustaka/docs/product/brd.html`,
domain L.
